    "language": "[0][1]I have the ball. Prepare to pass to the open right winger. Move up to support the winger after pass. [2]Move forward to support and provide a passing option. [3][4]So right now, you need to evaluate all of your passing options before you pass. Your right striker was blocked but I think there might've been a path to your left striker, so you should go forward if you can. If you cannot however, your right winger is a good option, and when you p- provide a supporting option, you don't necessarily need to go forward. You just wanna be within a five-feet radius of them that's, uh, that has a path between you and the, the winger or striker, your teammate, that's unobstructed by a defender.[5]",
